{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 36, "timestamp": 1792296412, "idle_time_limit": 2.5, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "dumb"}, "title": "sub-session demo (toy hello-notes repo)"}
[0.060095, "o", "\r\n============================================================\r\n  sub-session demo  —  throwaway repo: hello-notes\r\n  MASTER = this shell\r\n  SEAT   = a second clone, standing in for another tool\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n"]
[2.060891, "o", "-- SEAT: arm inbox watcher (P=5, NOTIFY_ECHO, ON_CHANGE) --\r\n"]
[3.06207, "o", "-- MASTER: arm outbox watcher (P=5, NOTIFY_ECHO) --\r\n"]
[5.062873, "o", "-- watchers as they armed --\r\n"]
[5.06474, "o", "   seat | NO INBOX AT collab/INBOX_review.md ON main. The watcher will keep polling and will pick it up the moment it appears, but if that path is a typo it will wait for ever. Check the name against what the master actually writes.\r\n   seat | inbox watcher cold start: changes before now are invisible to it, and the check-in's watermark range query is what recovers them. The current inbox follows, capped at 120 lines, so it is at least in this log:\r\n   seat | (no inbox at that path yet)\r\n   seat | and this watcher can start a turn, so that inbox is treated as UNDELIVERED and the first poll will deliver it rather than recording it as handled\r\n   seat | inbox watcher ARMED on main at head none, inbox blob none, P=5, running script 597b8c89\r\n   seat | the acknowledgement gate is OFF, so a turn that ends is recorded handled. That proves a turn ENDED and not that the instruction was carried out. Set ACK_BRANCH to the seat's branch to require its acknowledgement.\r\n   seat | notifications are ON through: sh /tmp/subsession-demo/notify-tee.sh \"Master shell\" \"Seat clone\"\r\n"]
[5.065327, "o", " master | outbox watcher cold start, seeded at 0 entries: anything pushed before now is invisible to it, recover with the range query\r\n master | notifications are ON through: sh /tmp/subsession-demo/notify-tee.sh \"Seat clone\" \"Master shell\"\r\n master | outbox watcher ARMED on work/review at head none, 0 entries, P=5, running script e0fa0a92\r\n"]
[5.065781, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.066704, "o", "-- MASTER: write REVIEW-1 and push --\r\n"]
[6.090224, "o", "   pushed INBOX_review.md on main\r\n"]
[7.09117, "o", "-- waiting for the seat (one poll, P=5) --\r\n"]
[10.097908, "o", "\r\n-- SEAT watcher (inbox change + turn) --\r\n"]
[10.098366, "o", "   seat | NO INBOX AT collab/INBOX_review.md ON main. The watcher will keep polling and will pick it up the moment it appears, but if that path is a typo it will wait for ever. Check the name against what the master actually writes.\r\n   seat | inbox watcher cold start: changes before now are invisible to it, and the check-in's watermark range query is what recovers them. The current inbox follows, capped at 120 lines, so it is at least in this log:\r\n   seat | (no inbox at that path yet)\r\n   seat | and this watcher can start a turn, so that inbox is treated as UNDELIVERED and the first poll will deliver it rather than recording it as handled\r\n   seat | inbox watcher ARMED on main at head none, inbox blob none, P=5, running script 597b8c89\r\n   seat | the acknowledgement gate is OFF, so a turn that ends is recorded handled. That proves a turn ENDED and not that the instruction was carried out. Set ACK_BRANCH to the seat's branch to require its acknowledgement.\r\n   seat | notifications are ON through: sh /tmp/subsession-demo/notify-tee.sh \"Master shell\" \"Seat clone\"\r\n   seat | INBOX CHANGED:\r\n   seat | ## Open instructions\r\n   seat | \r\n   seat | - REVIEW-1: add a heading to notes.txt. Gate: the file starts with #.\r\n   seat | starting a turn: sh /tmp/subsession-demo/seat-turn.sh\r\n   seat | the turn finished\r\n"]
[10.098443, "o", "\r\n-- SEAT outbox --\r\n"]
[10.099521, "o", "   - 2026-10-18 04:06:59 UTC REVIEW-1 started. Adding a heading to notes.txt.\r\n   - 2026-10-18 04:06:59 UTC REVIEW-1 done. Heading added.\r\n"]
[10.09963, "o", "\r\n"]
[11.103205, "o", "-- MASTER watcher (new outbox entries) --\r\n"]
[11.104121, "o", " master | outbox watcher cold start, seeded at 0 entries: anything pushed before now is invisible to it, recover with the range query\r\n master | notifications are ON through: sh /tmp/subsession-demo/notify-tee.sh \"Seat clone\" \"Master shell\"\r\n master | outbox watcher ARMED on work/review at head none, 0 entries, P=5, running script e0fa0a92\r\n master | OUTBOX new entries:\r\n master | - 2026-10-18 04:06:59 UTC REVIEW-1 started. Adding a heading to notes.txt.\r\n master | - 2026-10-18 04:06:59 UTC REVIEW-1 done. Heading added.\r\n"]
[11.104357, "o", "\r\n-- notification lines (NOTIFY_ECHO via notify.sh) --\r\n"]
[11.105016, "o", "   Master shell → Seat clone\r\n   started\r\n   an inbox change arrived, starting a turn\r\n   Seat clone → Master shell\r\n   finished\r\n   the turn ended, its report is the seat's to push\r\n   Seat clone → Master shell\r\n   finished\r\n   2 new outbox entries\r\n"]
[11.105163, "o", "============================================================\r\n  done. The seat received the instruction, replied, and a\r\n  notification printed. Toy repo discarded after the GIF.\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n"]
